      {
        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Lock in KPI set, targets, and reporting cadence for the dashboard.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 91858,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, moving on to `T5`. I've put together a draft 'Quality KPI Dictionary and Dashboard Spec' in `A3`. It proposes a set of core KPIs to track quality performance consistently across all sites. Please review and provide your thoughts.",
            "mentions": [
              436982
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T5",
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 436982,
            "reply_to": "M41",
            "text": "Taking a look now.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 436982,
            "reply_to": "M42",
            "text": "The list in `A3` has First Pass Yield, Scrap Rate, and Customer Complaints. Should we also add Training Completion Rate?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 91858,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "That's a good thought. However, Training Completion is a project-specific, one-time metric for the rollout itself. The KPIs in `A3` are meant for ongoing, long-term operational monitoring. We want to keep the dashboard focused on 3-5 core process health indicators to avoid information overload.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M45",
            "speaker_id": 436982,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "Ah, I see. That makes sense. So we should stick to operational metrics.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M46",
            "speaker_id": 91858,
            "reply_to": "M45",
            "text": "Exactly. Based on our project objectives, I propose we finalize this core list: 'First Pass Yield', 'Non-Conformance Rate' (instead of Scrap, as it's broader), and 'On-Time Delivery'. This gives us a view of quality, compliance, and efficiency.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M47",
            "speaker_id": 436982,
            "reply_to": "M46",
            "text": "I agree with those three. They cover the key areas.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M48",
            "speaker_id": 91858,
            "reply_to": "M47",
            "text": "Great. Let's make that official then. We are finalizing the core KPI list and their definitions as documented in `A3`.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_check_mark",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M49",
            "speaker_id": 91858,
            "reply_to": "M48",
            "text": "Next, we need to decide on the reporting cadence and data owners. This is crucial for `T10` when we build the dashboard.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T10"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M50",
            "speaker_id": 91858,
            "reply_to": "M49",
            "text": "I suggest a monthly reporting cadence. It's frequent enough to spot trends but not so frequent that it becomes a burden. For owners, the Site Supervisors at each location would be responsible for providing the raw data.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M51",
            "speaker_id": 436982,
            "reply_to": "M50",
            "text": "Monthly sounds right. Who will collect the data from them and create the report?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M52",
            "speaker_id": 91858,
            "reply_to": "M51",
            "text": "I'd like you to be the central owner for compiling the data and updating the dashboard each month. Does that work for you?",
            "mentions": [
              436982
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M53",
            "speaker_id": 436982,
            "reply_to": "M52",
            "text": "Yes, I can do that. I'll need to know where to get the data from at each site.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M54",
            "speaker_id": 91858,
            "reply_to": "M53",
            "text": "We'll document the specific data sources for each KPI in `A3` as part of `T10`. For now, let's confirm the decision on cadence and ownership.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3",
              "T10"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D6"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M55",
            "speaker_id": 436982,
            "reply_to": "M54",
            "text": "Confirmed. Monthly cadence, Site Supervisors provide data, I compile it.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M56",
            "speaker_id": 91858,
            "reply_to": "M55",
            "text": "Perfect. `D5` and `D6` are now locked in. I will update `A3` with these decisions. Your next step will be to start the detailed design for the dashboard as part of `T10`.",
